{"id":"CVE-2020-8252","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2020-09-18T20:11:51.000Z","updated":"2025-04-30T22:24:26.861Z","description":"The implementation of realpath in libuv < 10.22.1, < 12.18.4, and < 14.9.0 used within Node.js incorrectly determined the buffer size which can result in a buffer overflow if the resolved path is longer than 256 bytes.","cwe":["CWE-120 Classic Buffer Overflow (CWE-120)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"NodeJS","product":"Node","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 4.0 <4.* (semver)","affected 5.0 <5.* (semver)","affected 6.0 <6.* (semver)","affected 7.0 <7.* (semver)","affected 8.0 <8.* (semver)","affected 9.0 <9.* (semver)","affected 10.0 <10.22.1 (semver)","affected 11.0 <11.* (semver)","affected 12.0 <12.18.4 (semver)","affected 13.0 <13.* (semver)","affected 14.0 <14.9.0 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/september-2020-security-releases/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/965914","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202009-15","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202009-15"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/4548-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-4548-1"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2020-10/msg00011.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2020:1616"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20201009-0004/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2020-10/msg00023.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2020:1660"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/4OOYAMJVLLCLXDTHW3V5UXNULZBBK4O6/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2020-43d5a372fc"}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-8265","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2021-01-06T21:01:15.000Z","updated":"2025-04-30T22:24:28.624Z","description":"Node.js versions before 10.23.1, 12.20.1, 14.15.4, 15.5.1 are vulnerable to a use-after-free bug in its TLS implementation. When writing to a TLS enabled socket, node::StreamBase::Write calls node::TLSWrap::DoWrite with a freshly allocated WriteWrap object as first argument. If the DoWrite method does not return an error, this object is passed back to the caller as part of a StreamWriteResult structure. This may be exploited to corrupt memory leading to a Denial of Service or potentially other exploits.","cwe":["CWE-416 Use After Free (CWE-416)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"NodeJS","product":"Node","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 4.0 <4.* (semver)","affected 5.0 <5.* (semver)","affected 6.0 <6.* (semver)","affected 7.0 <7.* (semver)","affected 8.0 <8.* (semver)","affected 9.0 <9.* (semver)","affected 10.0 <10.23.1 (semver)","affected 11.0 <11.* (semver)","affected 12.0 <12.20.1 (semver)","affected 13.0 <13.* (semver)","affected 14.0 <14.15.4 (semver)","affected 15.0 <15.5.1 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/january-2021-security-releases/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/988103","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2021/dsa-4826","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4826"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/K4I6MZNC7C7VIDQR267OL4TVCI3ZKAC4/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2021-fb1a136393"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202101-07","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202101-07"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/H472D5HPXN6RRXCNFML3BK5OYC52CXF2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2021-d5b2c18fe6"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpujan2021.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20210212-0003/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/pdf/ssa-389290.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-8277","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2020-11-19T00:32:13.000Z","updated":"2025-04-30T22:24:27.745Z","description":"A Node.js application that allows an attacker to trigger a DNS request for a host of their choice could trigger a Denial of Service in versions < 15.2.1, < 14.15.1, and < 12.19.1 by getting the application to resolve a DNS record with a larger number of responses. This is fixed in 15.2.1, 14.15.1, and 12.19.1.","cwe":["CWE-400 Denial of Service (CWE-400)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"NodeJS","product":"Node","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 4.0 <4.* (semver)","affected 5.0 <5.* (semver)","affected 6.0 <6.* (semver)","affected 7.0 <7.* (semver)","affected 8.0 <8.* (semver)","affected 9.0 <9.* (semver)","affected 11.0 <11.* (semver)","affected 12.0 <12.19.1 (semver)","affected 13.0 <13.* (semver)","affected 14.0 <14.15.1 (semver)","affected 15.0 <15.2.1 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/1033107","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/november-2020-security-releases/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/A7WH7W46OZSEUHWBHD7TCH3LRFY52V6Z/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2020-7473744de1"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/BEJBY3RJB3XWUOJFGZM5E3EMQ7MFM3UT/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2020-307e873389"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202012-11","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202012-11"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202101-07","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202101-07"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpujan2021.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list