{"id":"CVE-2020-13822","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2020-06-04T14:01:53.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T12:25:16.506Z","description":"The Elliptic package 6.5.2 for Node.js allows ECDSA signature malleability via variations in encoding, leading '\\0' bytes, or integer overflows. This could conceivably have a security-relevant impact if an application relied on a single canonical signature.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/elliptic","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/indutny/elliptic/issues/226","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://yondon.blog/2019/01/01/how-not-to-use-ecdsa/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://medium.com/%40herman_10687/malleability-attack-why-it-matters-7b5f59fb99a4","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-14966","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2020-06-22T11:20:13.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T13:00:52.168Z","description":"An issue was discovered in the jsrsasign package through 8.0.18 for Node.js. It allows a malleability in ECDSA signatures by not checking overflows in the length of a sequence and '0' characters appended or prepended to an integer. The modified signatures are verified as valid. This could have a security-relevant impact if an application relied on a single canonical signature.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://kjur.github.io/jsrsasign/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/jsrsasign","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/issues/437","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/releases/tag/8.0.18","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/releases/tag/8.0.17","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20200724-0001/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-14967","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2020-06-22T11:19:35.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T13:00:52.090Z","description":"An issue was discovered in the jsrsasign package before 8.0.18 for Node.js. Its RSA PKCS1 v1.5 decryption implementation does not detect ciphertext modification by prepending '\\0' bytes to ciphertexts (it decrypts modified ciphertexts without error). An attacker might prepend these bytes with the goal of triggering memory corruption issues.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://kjur.github.io/jsrsasign/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/jsrsasign","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/releases/tag/8.0.18","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/releases/tag/8.0.17","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/issues/439","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20200724-0001/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-14968","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2020-06-22T11:19:49.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T13:00:52.147Z","description":"An issue was discovered in the jsrsasign package before 8.0.17 for Node.js. Its RSASSA-PSS (RSA-PSS) implementation does not detect signature manipulation/modification by prepending '\\0' bytes to a signature (it accepts these modified signatures as valid). An attacker can abuse this behavior in an application by creating multiple valid signatures where only one signature should exist. Also, an attacker might prepend these bytes with the goal of triggering memory corruption issues.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://kjur.github.io/jsrsasign/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/jsrsasign","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/releases/tag/8.0.18","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/releases/tag/8.0.17","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/issues/438","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20200724-0001/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-15779","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2020-07-15T20:42:39.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T13:22:30.824Z","description":"A Path Traversal issue was discovered in the socket.io-file package through 2.0.31 for Node.js. The socket.io-file::createFile message uses path.join with ../ in the name option, and the uploadDir and rename options determine the path.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/socket.io-file","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/rico345100/socket.io-file","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/advisories/1519","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9h4g-27m8-qjrg","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-24660","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2020-09-14T12:51:48.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T15:19:09.076Z","description":"An issue was discovered in LemonLDAP::NG through 2.0.8, when NGINX is used. An attacker may bypass URL-based access control to protected Virtual Hosts by submitting a non-normalized URI. This also affects versions before 0.5.2 of the \"Lemonldap::NG handler for Node.js\" package.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://gitlab.ow2.org/lemonldap-ng/lemonldap-ng/-/issues/2290","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2020/dsa-4762","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4762"},{"url":"https://github.com/LemonLDAPNG/node-lemonldap-ng-handler/security/advisories/GHSA-x44x-r84w-8v67","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/LemonLDAPNG/node-lemonldap-ng-handler/releases/tag/0.5.2","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-24807","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2020-10-06T17:10:17.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T15:19:09.430Z","description":"The socket.io-file package through 2.0.31 for Node.js relies on client-side validation of file types, which allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code by uploading an executable file via a modified JSON name field. NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/socket.io-file","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/rico345100/socket.io-file","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/advisories/1564","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6495-8jvh-f28x","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-27543","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2021-02-25T16:15:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T16:18:44.839Z","description":"The restify-paginate package 0.0.5 for Node.js allows remote attackers to cause a Denial-of-Service by omitting the HTTP Host header. A Restify-based web service would crash with an uncaught exception.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/restify-paginate","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/paulvarache/restify-paginate/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/secoats/cve/tree/master/CVE-2020-27543_dos_restify-paginate","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20210401-0002/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-36732","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2023-06-12T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-01-06T17:45:13.240Z","description":"The crypto-js package before 3.2.1 for Node.js generates random numbers by concatenating the string \"0.\" with an integer, which makes the output more predictable than necessary.","cwe":["n/a","CWE-331 CWE-331 Insufficient Entropy"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":5.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JS-CRYPTOJS-548472"},{"url":"https://github.com/brix/crypto-js/pull/257/commits/e4ac157d8b75b962d6538fc0b996e5d4d5a9466b"},{"url":"https://github.com/brix/crypto-js/issues/254"},{"url":"https://github.com/brix/crypto-js/issues/256"},{"url":"https://github.com/brix/crypto-js/compare/3.2.0...3.2.1"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20230706-0003/"}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
